}
if (state.pending) ctx.requestNextFrame();
ctx.output("image", state.image);
if (captured) ctx.pulse("captured");
```

- What's captured: the frame as drawn at the end of the Capture frame, after this frame's layer changes, so a layer shown on the same frame is included. The layer and its descendants are drawn into the layer's own bounds: the layer's own position, anchor, scale, rotation, and opacity are ignored, its children keep theirs, and anything outside the bounds (including spilling shadows) is clipped. An empty Layer captures the root artboard at device size, background included.
- Pixels: at `device().screenScale` pixels per point, in Display P3 where the platform supports it, as a PNG with transparency, output as `{ url: "blob:…" }`. Captures larger than 8192 px on a side are scaled down to fit.
- Limits: 3D rotations inside the layer are flattened. Shader layers are included. In the web player, images and videos from other sites without CORS headers draw as transparent.
- Pulses: `capture`. Pulses on consecutive frames each start a capture, but only the newest request's result is applied, so a burst gives one Captured pulse.
- Frame 0: Image is null. A Capture pulse on frame 0 captures the first drawn frame.
- Edge cases: a missing layer fails, so Image keeps the previous picture and one warning is logged. A hidden layer (Enabled off or opacity 0) captures a transparent picture of its size. A layer with zero width or height fails the same way as a missing layer.
- Loops: per index. A loop of layer references (instances of a looped layer) captures each instance separately.
- Muted: no captures; Image is null.
- Platform and simulation: the renderer draws the layer's subtree offscreen at the capture size. The desktop app renders the same DOM offscreen and reads real pixels; the web player redraws the SceneFrame into a canvas. Headless simulation can't draw pixels: Capture logs `snapshot: no renderer in simulation` once per restart and Image stays null.
- Platform contract: `platform.snapshot(layer, { scale })` resolves with the picture.
- Restart and dispose: Image clears, pending results are dropped, and every blob URL this patch created is revoked.
- Coming from Origami: Origami's Sample pulse is `capture`. Origami notes that some layer transformations don't capture; Sonobe's rule is the one above.

