- Detection passes: a pass starts when none is in flight and the layer shows a new frame (a changed picture, or a new video or camera frame). At Low, pictures are downscaled so the longest side is at most 640 px and at most 10 passes run per second; at High, every new frame runs at full size. Results apply on the first frame after the pass finishes, and outputs hold the latest results in between. Results of superseded passes (Layer changed, disabled, restart) are dropped.
- Coordinates: detectors report boxes and points in picture pixels, origin top-left, y down. Absolute outputs those. Relative maps them into the layer's parent space using where the picture sits inside the layer and the layer's previous-frame geometry from `services.layerInfo`: `local = contentOrigin + p × contentScale`, then `parent = position − anchor × size × scale + local × scale`, and sizes multiply by `contentScale × scale`. Layer rotation is ignored. With picture size cw × ch in a layer w × h: Fill uses `s = max(w / cw, h / ch)` centered, Fit uses `s = min(w / cw, h / ch)` centered, Stretch scales x by `w / cw` and y by `h / ch`, and Tile uses 1 at the top-left.
